<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Banco Rio plans $580 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Banco Rio plans $580 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Banco Rio de la Plata said Tuesday that it has decided to issue a fifth and sixth series of bonds in dollars for $500 million and $80 million respectively.</p>
<p>The issues will be part of the bank's global bond program, Banco Rio said in a letter to the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange.  </p>
<p>Banco Rio said it has applied to Argentina's National Securities Commission to authorize an expansion of its global bond program.</p>
<p>Banco Rio is controlled by Spain's Banco Santander .</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
